        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: حريق",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "حريق — ḥarīq — \"a blaze, a fire that spreads\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "رأى الجيران حريقا في المصنع. raʾā al-jīrān ḥarīqan fī al-maṣnaʿ. The neighbours saw a fire at the factory."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "نار is fire itself; حريق (ḥarīq) is a fire that destroys."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "حريق (ḥarīq) is built on the native Arabic root ḥ-r-q (Lane), \"to burn\". Ḥarīq is the fire that burns a thing up."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling what happened."
